 One month in the life of a demo company. The scenario runs every
 subledger against a single general ledger: procure-to-pay,
 make-to-stock, order-to-cash, payroll, cost allocation, and a
 month-end close, then renders the trial balance and statements.
 This chapter deliberately defines no opening; the battery test and
 the bootable demo both cite it and provide their own entry points.

 The demo company CODEX in period 6 of 2026: capitalized with
 5000000 cash, buys 100 units of raw material RM1 at 5000, makes 40
 finished units FG1 (two RM1 each plus 1500 absorbed labor, standard
 cost 11500), sells 30 at 20000, runs one payroll, allocates IT cost
 to sales, buys a 480000 machine depreciating straight-line over 48
 months, and closes the period.

